WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.203
-Welcome back, guys.
It is time for "Bad Signs."

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.671
Here we go.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:07.407
-♪ We lucky we got 'em ♪

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.841
♪♪

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:15.982
♪ Bad si-i-i-gns ♪

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.616
-Alright, here we go.
Very nice.

00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:20.119
These are -- These are pictures
of funny or weird signs

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.021
that you guys saw
and sent in to us.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.355
They are all real.

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:24.390
This first one was sent in

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.825
by Samantha English
in Canton, Ohio.

00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:30.963
She was using a restaurant
bathroom and spotted this.

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:33.533
"Employees must 'wash hands.'"

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.702
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.103
-Yeah.
-Hey, man.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.838
-"Yeah, I 'washed my hands.'
Look."

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.040
-Yeah.
-"And I 'flushed the toilet.'"

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.110
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.613
-This next one was sent in...
[ Laughs ]

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.816
...sent in by Jeff Dutton
in Los Angeles, California.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.117
-Ooh.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.319
-He was looking for something
to eat, and he saw this.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.055
"Soup of the Day:
Beef Barely Soup."

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:59.425
Well, there you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.960
If you're on a strict --
it's barely soup.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.562
-Yeah.
-It's more of a sandwich.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:06.132
-Yeah. A runny sandwich.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.134
-"It's a pre-dipped French dip."

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.469
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.704
-With no beef.
-With no beef or bread.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.440
Now, this next one
is from Angie Cyphers

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.875
in Flat Rock, Michigan.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.544
She saw an Arby's sign.
I love Arby's.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.578
Let's see what it said here.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.747
It said, "Now hiring anybody."

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.315
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:23.582
[ Applause ]
Wow.

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.684
-Wow.
-Anybody.

00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:28.721
-[ Laughs ]
-Come on in!

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.656
-"The body's still warm."
-Yeah.

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:31.724
-"Do you want to be
the fry machine,

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.125
or do you want to work this?"

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:35.662
"Sure, I'll do fries."

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.564
-The next one's
from Marsha Lee Sparhawk

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.864
in Rigby, Idaho.

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:40.900
She spotted this while driving.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.971
"Speed limit --
5.37 miles per hour."

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.139
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:49.275
"Sorry, Officer,
I was going 5.39.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.210
My wife's in labor.
She's having a baby.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.379
So I was speeding a little bit."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:56.081
This next one
is from Farel Rooska

00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:58.318
in San Marcos, California.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.954
She was shopping for some wine
in Trader Joe's,

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.922
and they were
all out of Chardonnay.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.090
-Ohh.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:08.928
But they did have "Chadonnay."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.363
-Chadonnay, yeah.
-Oh, dude.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.497
-What's food -- If you want,

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:12.965
just grab a good Chad
and have...

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:14.734
-Yeah, man.
-Love Chad. Love a Chad.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.336
-Yeah.
-Ruby red.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.669
-Chad and chow, man.
-Yeah.

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:22.074
-This next one's from Beth Monte
in Snow Hill, Maryland.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:24.744
She was shopping
in a bakery and saw this.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.045
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.548
"Please use tongues
to pick pastries up. Thanks."

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.716
[ Audience ewws ]
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:33.052
"Well, I 'washed my hands.'"
-Yeah.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.254
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:36.589
-"Got a little bit."
-"No, I don't want that one."

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.857
-Yeah. "Maybe this one."

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.425
-"Buddy, I don't --
I don't like all that."

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.793
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.194
"That --
Oh, that's too expensive.

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:43.396
That's $3,000."

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.764
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.367
The next one's from Dave Riggins
in Hillside, New Jersey.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.902
He was getting kind of hungry,
so he stopped by a local market.

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.237
Let's see what they had here.

00:02:52.237 --> 00:02:53.605
"Lynda's Market: Lunch special.

00:02:53.605 --> 00:02:54.707
We have worms."

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.076
Oh, there you go.
[ Audience ohs ]

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.445
-"Oh!"
-"Oh!"

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.047
"Hey, baby."
-That sounds delicious,

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.349
but I'll stick
to my beef barely soup.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.417
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:06.819
Well, this next one here

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.656
is from Jacob Brelsford
in Telluride, Colorado.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.657
He was out for a walk
and saw this.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:13.459
"Please do not sit on fence."

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:16.862
Well, you know, hey, go for it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:19.231
Go for it. Never mind.
Just sit --

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.533
"Dad, you want to sit
on this fence with me?

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.801
And we'll talk about life
and stuff."

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.202
"Yeah.
All right, you go first."

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.371
[ Groans ]
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:29.241
Here's one from Whitney Wilding
in Clinton, New Jersey.

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:31.443
She was shopping
for some plastic bins.

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:33.546
Let's see what she found.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.614
Oh, "NObreak"
is the name of the brand.

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:38.384
It's -- It's interesting
'cause they're all broken.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.453
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.187
Maybe they're ironic.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.187 --> 00:03:43.656
-It's the ir--
-NObreak, yeah.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.924
-"NObreak."

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.626
And finally, this last sign

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:49.995
is from Tim Kubinak
in Suffolk, Virginia.

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:52.431
He was in the grocery store
and spotted a new product

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:54.099
for Thomas' English Muffins...
-Oh.

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:55.635
-...from
Thomas' English Muffins.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:57.469
But look -- look at where
they put the coupon.

00:03:57.469 --> 00:04:00.273
Look at this.
-Ah!

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:03.375
-"Pick Me -- Pick Me Ups."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:04.877
"Pick -- Pick Me Ups."

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.412
[ Laughter and applause ]
"Pick Me Up."

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.247
That's all the time we have
for "Bad Signs."

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.515
If you see a funny sign,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.285
e-mail it to us at
BadSigns@TonightShow.com,

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.553
and we might put it on the show.

